# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

/target

# Default --workdir. Holds probe sources, artifacts, and captured stdout/stderr,
# which are retained deliberately as evidence for a run but are outputs, not
# sources.
/chard-work
*.stdout
*.stderr

# A third-party reference document, fetched rather than vendored: its licence has
# not been verified for redistribution and it is not needed to build or run chard.
# Fetch it with: curl -sSL -o compiler-flags-distro-README.md \
#   'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jvoisin/compiler-flags-distro/main/README.md'
/compiler-flags-distro-README.md

# Sweep outputs: downloaded distribution images, per-image guest working
# directories, and the JSON reports a run produces. A glob rather than an
# enumeration, because the previous list was one-name-per-directory and had
# already fallen behind the harness that writes them: it produces
# `chard-bare-out` and `chard-vm-bare`, and neither was ignored.
/chard-images
/chard-vm*
/chard-*-out
/chard-out*
/archive

# Working notes that name this development host: absolute paths, image cache
# locations, sweep output directories. Tracked files stay host-free (see the
# "Scrub the development host out of the tree" commit), so anything that has to
# record where things live on a particular machine goes here instead.
*.private.md

# The leak gate's private pattern list: the names and host-only paths that identify a
# developer's machine, which `scripts/leak-gate.sh` scans the object graph for. Ignored
# because the list is the disclosure: tracked, it would publish every name it exists to
# keep out. Each machine holds its own; the script's header says how to write one. The glob
# covers a copy or backup made beside it.
/scripts/leak-gate.private*

# Editor detritus. Not merely untidy: a swap file is a binary snapshot of whatever was
# being edited, and its header records the editing user and host by construction, so one
# committed here publishes the development machine. `scripts/leak-gate.sh` scans the object
# graph rather than the checkout, since an ignore rule leaves exposed whatever was committed
# before it.
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Agent working configuration: local tool permissions and session settings. Untracked, and
# ignored so that a single `git add -A` does not commit it.
.claude/
# Output of `make clang`, removed by `make clean`.
chard-clang.json
# `cargo mutants` working output.
mutants.out*/
# aarch64 bring-up notes: predictions, the results measured against them, and the sweep
# reports behind those results. Kept locally as evidence of a forecast made before the
# measurement; untracked because the repository does not publish per-toolchain results.
docs/bringup/

# Review findings kept at the checkout root, not published.
FINDINGS.md
